Although very different approaches for the optimization of lipase-catalyzed reactions have been discussed in this review, they all have the same aim: a perfect biocatalytic process. Indeed, a single application of only one of these methods will not lead to the optimal process, what is needed is a skilled combination of several different strategies.An enzyme optimized by molecular biology methods for efficient activity and/or stereoselectivity still, in most cases, needs to be adapted to process conditions and, as a consequence, the physicochemical and reaction engineering methods will remain important in future developments.
